WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.292 --> 00:00:16.694
danced around the nursery with joy, and Tinker Bell followed his every move.

2
00:00:18.155 --> 00:00:19.055
They ignored Mr.

3
00:00:19.075 --> 00:00:21.476
Darling asleep in Nana's dog house.

4
00:00:22.617 --> 00:00:25.898
Peter peeked into the other room to see who was playing the piano.

5
00:00:26.779 --> 00:00:29.620
He whispered to Tink, "That's Wendy's mother.

6
00:00:31.688 --> 00:00:34.850
She's a pretty lady, but not as pretty as Wendy."

7
00:00:36.231 --> 00:00:39.974
All of a sudden, the music stopped, and Peter saw that Mrs.

8
00:00:40.014 --> 00:00:41.075
Darling was crying.

9
00:00:42.216 --> 00:00:44.057
Her heart seemed to be broken.

10
00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:49.521
"She wants me to open the window," thought Peter, "but I won't!"

11
00:00:50.641 --> 00:00:54.564
Peter took a step closer and saw the tears shining on her cheeks.

12
00:00:56.866 --> 00:00:59.628
"She's awfully fond of Wendy," he thought.

13
00:01:00.748 --> 00:01:03.751
Then he said stubbornly, "But so am I!"

14
00:01:04.932 --> 00:01:09.275
Mrs. Darling continued to cry, and Peter couldn't look at her anymore.

15
00:01:10.476 --> 00:01:13.999
He skipped about and made funny faces, but this didn't help.

16
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.682
He began to feel sorry for her.

17
00:01:16.702 --> 00:01:22.387
"Oh, all right," he said at last and opened the window.

18
00:01:22.407 --> 00:01:25.369
"Come on, Tink," he called.

19
00:01:25.389 --> 00:01:28.572
"We don't want any silly mothers anyway."

20
00:01:29.608 --> 00:01:32.511
And he and Tinker Bell flew out the window again.

21
00:01:33.832 --> 00:01:39.436
When Wendy, John, and Michael arrived, they found the window open, just as Mrs.

22
00:01:39.476 --> 00:01:40.697
Darling had left it for them.

23
00:01:42.338 --> 00:01:44.060
They flew in and looked around.

24
00:01:46.021 --> 00:01:48.463
Everything in the nursery looked very familiar.

25
00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:52.647
"I think I've been here before," said Michael.

26
00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:55.249
"Of course you have, silly.

27
00:01:55.269 --> 00:01:58.992
There is your old bed," said Wendy, pointing.

28
00:02:00.736 --> 00:02:05.179
"So it is," said Michael, as though he really remembered.

29
00:02:05.199 --> 00:02:10.542
"And look," cried John, "there's Nana's dog house.

30
00:02:11.462 --> 00:02:13.143
Perhaps Nana is in there."

31
00:02:13.683 --> 00:02:14.424
He went to look.

32
00:02:15.724 --> 00:02:17.705
"There's a man inside!"

33
00:02:18.306 --> 00:02:20.227
he said in a surprised voice.

34
00:02:20.247 --> 00:02:22.748
"It's Father!"

35
00:02:23.389 --> 00:02:24.129
cried Wendy.

36
00:02:24.149 --> 00:02:27.931
"Let me look at him," Michael begged.

37
00:02:28.451 --> 00:02:29.572
He took a good look.

38
00:02:30.688 --> 00:02:36.393
"He's not as big as the pirate I killed in Neverland," he said with disappointment.

39
00:02:37.514 --> 00:02:38.875
Thankfully, Mr.

40
00:02:38.915 --> 00:02:41.317
Darling was still asleep and did not hear him.

41
00:02:43.118 --> 00:02:51.005
"Surely," said John, who had lost faith in his own memory, "Father didn't always sleep in a dog

42
00:02:51.065 --> 00:02:54.067
house." Just then Mrs.

43
00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.189
Darling started to play the piano again.

44
00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:59.912
"That must be Mother," cried Wendy.

45
00:03:01.228 --> 00:03:03.910
"Then you're not really our mother, Wendy?"

46
00:03:04.671 --> 00:03:05.331
asked Michael.

47
00:03:06.492 --> 00:03:09.875
Wendy looked at Michael in a wistful way and patted his head.

48
00:03:09.895 --> 00:03:13.999
"Let's surprise Mother," suggested John.

49
00:03:14.019 --> 00:03:19.363
"We'll put our hands over her eyes and ask her to guess who we are."

50
00:03:20.885 --> 00:03:23.046
Wendy thought they should break the news more gently.

51
00:03:23.967 --> 00:03:26.850
"Let's get into our beds," she suggested.

52
00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:31.269
"We'll be there when she comes in, as if we had never left."

53
00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:38.035
The children all ran to their beds and jumped between the sheets, pulling the covers up to their

54
00:03:38.115 --> 00:03:40.677
chins. When Mrs.

55
00:03:40.697 --> 00:03:45.741
Darling went back to the nursery to see if her husband was still asleep, all the beds were

56
00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:50.825
filled. The children waited for her cry of joy, but it didn't come.

57
00:03:52.326 --> 00:03:57.351
She had dreamed so many times that her children were still in their beds that she thought this

58
00:03:57.471 --> 00:03:58.712
was just another dream.

59
00:04:00.488 --> 00:04:05.389
As she had often done before, she sat in the chair by the fire and closed her eyes.

60
00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:07.970
The children were disappointed.

61
00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:10.531
"Mother!" cried Wendy.

62
00:04:10.551 --> 00:04:13.852
"That's Wendy," said Mrs.

63
00:04:13.892 --> 00:04:15.912
Darling, sure it was her dream.

64
00:04:15.932 --> 00:04:19.133
"Mother!" cried John.

65
00:04:19.153 --> 00:04:22.634
"That's John," she said.

66
00:04:22.654 --> 00:04:25.835
"Mother!" cried Michael.

67
00:04:26.315 --> 00:04:27.115
He knew her now.

68
00:04:27.135 --> 00:04:30.452
"That's Michael," she said.

69
00:04:31.353 --> 00:04:32.894
Then she opened her eyes.

70
00:04:33.955 --> 00:04:37.818
And all three children jumped out of bed and ran into her arms.

71
00:04:37.838 --> 00:04:41.701
"George, George!"

72
00:04:42.341 --> 00:04:44.603
she cried, "The children are back!"

73
00:04:45.863 --> 00:04:49.826
Mr. Darling woke up in the dog house and Nana came rushing in.

74
00:04:50.907 --> 00:04:52.108
It was a beautiful sight.

75
00:04:53.169 --> 00:04:57.472
So beautiful, in fact, that it would have warmed the heart of anyone who looked on.

76
00:04:58.796 --> 00:05:03.704
But no one else was watching, no one except for a little boy staring through the window.
